{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210692,"nonce":"Wy3xE4A8p9Y3Yy8Ti/oSJz2YeVM=","title":"JIT and threaded interp cannot suspend a fiber mid-execution","message":"Functions that directly call Fiber.yield / suspend / try / transfer are pinned to the bytecode interpreter (2026-04-27). The JIT and threaded interp have no trampoline to unwind through native frames, so the pending_fiber_action dance cannot resume them.\n\nConsequence: any hot loop that yields (schedulers, generators, @hatch:web per-connection fibers) runs at interpreter speed. The AOT side has the same shape and is tracked under the krio-fiber issue; a krio-backed stackful fiber would let JIT'd bodies yield from any depth and would close this for native targets too.","files":null}]}